## Test that llvm-bolt handles PE/COFF binaries with CFG Guard (/GUARD:CF).
## In-place patching preserves function entry RVAs, keeping the GFids table valid.

# RUN: yaml2obj %p/Inputs/cfg-guard.yaml -o %t.exe
# RUN: llvm-bolt %t.exe -o %t.out.exe 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: processing PE/COFF binary
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: binary has Control Flow Guard (/GUARD:CF)
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: 2 functions discovered from .pdata
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: disassembled 2 functions
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: no profile data, producing identity copy
# CHECK-NOT: BOLT-ERROR
